### Notes on the SQLite dependency chain

`modernc.org/sqlite` is SQLite transpiled to Go rather than bound to it, which is
why the store needs no cgo. Its own code is BSD-3-Clause; the upstream SQLite
sources it is derived from are public domain, which imposes no obligation. The
chain pulls in `modernc.org/libc`, a Go translation of musl (MIT) — both licenses
are in the allowed set and both are reproduced in the modules' own `LICENSE` and
`LICENSE-3RD-PARTY.md` files.

One GPL-licensed file exists in that chain: `crlibm` test vectors under
`modernc.org/libc`'s `testdata/`. It is test data for that module's own test
suite, is not part of any package Xfuzz imports, and reaches no build of Xfuzz.
It is recorded here rather than omitted, because a policy that only lists what is
convenient is not a policy.
